 sharing this interesting work!\n\nI was curious about the actual playing strength of the PPO baselines in Experiment 6. While they achieve high win rates against random players, it's unclear whether they've learned meaningful Go strategies.\n\nWould it be possible to share a few sample games (e.g., SGF files) from the Astra vs. PPO evaluations? It would be helpful to see whether the PPO agents are making reasonable moves or mostly playing near-randomly.\n\nThanks!","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/3/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/3/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/2","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/2/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/2/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/2/events","html_url":"https://github.com/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/2","id":6175020057,"node_id":"I_kwDOVbUqvc8AAAABcA9UGQ","number":2,"title":"In awe","user":{"login":"mrconter1","id":32551374,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTUxMzc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32551374?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrconter1","html_url":"https://github.com/mrconter1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrconter1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrconter1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrconter1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrconter1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrconter1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrconter1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrconter1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrconter1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrconter1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-11-03T02:24:11Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T02:24:11Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I just wanted to say that I'm honestly in awe. I think you have cracked something genuinely astonishing and game changing. Incredible.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/2/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/2/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/pull/1","id":6174339479,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVbUqvc8AAAABMcmAHQ","number":1,"title":"Add Experiment 5 scorer: read a reply into a network and score it on MinAtar","user":{"login":"suitedaces","id":50865782,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwODY1Nzgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50865782?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces","html_url":"https://github.com/suitedaces","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/suitedaces/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-03T01:27:23Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T01:31:56Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/pulls/1","html_url":"https://github.com/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/pull/1","diff_url":"https://github.com/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/pull/1.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/pull/1.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"The release has the Experiment 5 replies, networks and scores, but no code to read a reply into a network or to score a network. This adds `exp5_write_from_scratch/code/score.py` and a short section in that folder's README.\n\n**What it does**\n- Reads a reply the way the prompt describes: only the last `edits` block, statements in order, a statement that cannot be read is skipped. It accepts the `[ [ ... ] ]` form mentioned in the README.\n- Scores a network with the protocol in the prompt: MinAtar 1.0.15, sticky actions 0.1, actions sampled from the softmax, at most 10,000 steps, 1,000 episodes. It prints the same fields as `eval/minatar_eval.json`.\n- `--save` writes the network read from a reply in the `hand.npz` format.\n\n**Checks**\n- Reading `runs/<game>/reply/answer.md` gives `networks/<game>/hand.npz` exactly (float32-identical), with the same statement counts as `apply.json` (92 / 122 / 55, 0 errors).\n- Scoring the released networks (seed 0):\n\n| Game | `eval/minatar_eval.json` | `code/score.py` |\n|---|---|---|\n| Breakout | 517.4 ± 7.4 | 502.8 ± 7.7 |\n| Seaquest | 53.1 ± 1.4 | 52.6 ± 1.4 |\n| Asterix | 53.2 ± 1.0 | 52.4 ± 1.0 |\n\nThe differences are within episode noise (different random streams for the game and the action sampling). If your scorer did anything differently, for example resetting `last_action` between episodes or a different seeding scheme, I'm happy to match it.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}]